From 526d5ca61674ec26745eed6994c3d9891484edf9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:04:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] screencast: offer converted 8-bit shm frames for 10-bit
 outputs

A compositor that renders an output in 10 bits (HDR, or 10-bit SDR) only
offers a 10-bit wl_shm capture format. Consumers that can neither import
dmabufs nor read 10-bit packed RGB, such as GStreamer's pipewiresrc and
with it RustDesk, then had no format in common with the stream: the link
failed with "no more input formats".

Offer XRGB8888 (BGRx) over shm as a last choice when the compositor has no
8-bit shm format. The frame is captured into a private 10-bit buffer and
converted into the buffer the consumer maps; only the regions that changed
since that buffer was last filled are converted, large ones on a few
threads. On a PQ output the frame is tone mapped to SDR: PQ is decoded, the
compositor's SDR reference white (from the output's image description)
becomes 1.0, BT.2020 becomes sRGB primaries and the result is encoded with
gamma 2.2, which is how wlroots puts untagged SDR surfaces on such an
output, so SDR content comes back as it went in. Light above reference
white clips.

Also stop exiting on every error the PipeWire core relays. Only a lost
connection is fatal; an error on one stream (such as the failed link above)
took all other screencasts and remote desktop sessions down with it.
